ReadReplaceQuote <pre><code>GET /api/orders/shipping-rates/
</code></pre> <p>Success (200):</p> <pre><code>{
  "countries": [
    { "country": "Kenya", "unit_weight": 1000, "fee": "20.00" }
  ]
}
</code></pre> <p>A new shop has <code>"countries": []</code>. <code>unit_weight</code> is grams. <code>fee</code> is USD for that many grams.</p> <pre><code>PUT /api/orders/shipping-rates/
</code></pre> <p>Admins only. This replaces the whole table. A country left out of <code>countries</code> is removed. The same rows can be edited one at a time in Django admin.</p> <pre><code>{
  "countries": [
    { "country": "Kenya", "unit_weight": 1000, "fee": "20.00" },
    { "country": "Nigeria", "unit_weight": 500, "fee": "15.00" }
  ]
}
</code></pre> <p>Success (200) returns the saved table. <code>fee</code> cannot be negative. <code>unit_weight</code> is at least 1 gram. The same country cannot be listed twice. Matching ignores letter case, so <code>kenya</code> and <code>Kenya</code> are one country.</p> <pre><code>POST /api/orders/shipping-rates/quote/
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "country": "Kenya",
  "items": [
    { "product": 1, "quantity": 1 },
    { "variant": 10, "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}
</code></pre> <p>Each item is a product or a variant, and a quantity of at least 1.</p> <p>Success (200):</p> <pre><code>{
  "country": "Kenya",
  "weight_grams": 500,
  "shipping_fee": "20.00"
}
</code></pre> <p><code>400</code> when the country is not on the schedule, or an item is missing.</p>

ListAddRead and update <pre><code>GET /api/users/staff/
</code></pre> <p>Example: 200 OK</p> <pre><code>[
  {
    "id": 4,
    "email": "ship@example.com",
    "phone": null,
    "first_name": "Sam",
    "last_name": "",
    "is_active": true,
    "is_staff": true,
    "is_superuser": false,
    "roles": ["Shipping"]
  }
]
</code></pre> <pre><code>POST /api/users/staff/
</code></pre> <p><code>email</code>, <code>password</code>, and <code>roles</code> are required. <code>roles</code> needs at least one of <code>Orders</code>, <code>Shipping</code>, <code>Stock</code>, and <code>Manager</code>. <code>first_name</code>, <code>last_name</code>, and <code>phone</code> are optional.</p> <pre><code>{
  "email": "ship@example.com",
  "password": "strongpass",
  "first_name": "Sam",
  "roles": ["Shipping", "Stock"]
}
</code></pre> <p>Example: 201 Created — The new staff user, with <code>roles</code> limited to the ticks in the request.</p> <p>Example: 400 Bad Request</p> <pre><code>{
  "roles": ["Choose at least one role."]
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>GET /api/users/staff/{id}/
PATCH /api/users/staff/{id}/
</code></pre> <p><code>PATCH</code> replaces the role ticks when <code>roles</code> is sent. <code>password</code> sets a new password. <code>is_active</code> can turn the account off. Email stays as it is.</p> <pre><code>{
  "roles": ["Shipping"],
  "is_active": true
}
</code></pre> <p>Example: 200 OK — The staff user after the change.</p> <p>Example: 404 Not Found</p> <pre><code>{
  "detail": "Not found."
}
</code></pre>
